          {
            "id": "c_idea0",
            "kind": "text",
            "html": "<h3>Every frame has a focal point</h3><p>Before you cut, ask where the eye lands first. Brightness, faces and contrast pull attention.</p>"
          },
          {
            "id": "c_idea1",
            "kind": "text",
            "html": "<h3>Thirds beat the centre</h3><p>Placing the subject on a third line leaves room to look into, and it feels more natural than dead centre.</p>"
          },
          {
            "id": "c_idea2",
            "kind": "text",
            "html": "<h3>Cut on movement</h3><p>A cut hidden inside a movement feels invisible, so the viewer stays in the story instead of noticing the edit.</p>"
          },
          {
            "id": "c_tip",
            "kind": "callout",
            "tone": "remember",
            "text": "If you have to ask where to look, the frame has no focal point yet."
          },
          {
